1
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:15,837
Back up!

2
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:16,760
Keep going!

3
00:00:17,480 --> 00:00:19,117
Who is it that you sense nearby weather?

4
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:22,477
Are you saying that Jolyne's
the one who's near the hospital?

5
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:25,757
Or do you mean the priest is
the person that's already here?

6
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:28,960
Actually, I can sense
three people, Anastasia.

7
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:30,657
Jolene is one of them.

8
00:00:30,740 --> 00:00:32,117
The priest is here, too.

9
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:33,788
But there is somebody else.

10
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:35,320
We gotta find them.

11
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:36,357
But where are they?

12
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:39,028
Could they be inside
one of these buildings?

13
00:00:41,060 --> 00:00:44,180
Excuse me, ladies. Welcome
aboard. Unfortunately,

14
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:46,377
this plane is expected
to lose control and crash

15
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:51,480
into the ground at approximately
21.33 on July Saudi, 2005.

16
00:00:56,080 --> 00:00:57,560
Hey, hold on.

17
00:00:57,700 --> 00:00:59,057
What do you think you're doing, Jolene?

18
00:00:59,140 --> 00:01:01,257
You're not planning on
opening that door, are you?

19
00:01:01,340 --> 00:01:03,637
I wasn't able to find
the exit on the ceiling.

20
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:08,485
So the fastest way to end this is to find
the stand user and attack him directly.

21
00:01:09,620 --> 00:01:11,757
Hermes, hold on tight to my rope again.

22
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:13,722
And strap yourself in somewhere.

23
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:15,697
And you, flight attendant lady,

24
00:01:15,780 --> 00:01:19,177
switch the settings on this door
so that I can open it manually.

25
00:01:19,260 --> 00:01:20,320
Yo, hang on.

26
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:23,817
It ain't exactly a good idea to open
the door when the plane's still moving,

27
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:24,730
you know?

28
00:01:24,813 --> 00:01:25,643
The air pressure would...

29
00:01:25,726 --> 00:01:26,556
Huh?

30
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:31,660
Nah, never mind!

31
00:01:31,980 --> 00:01:32,980
Go for it!

32
00:01:33,460 --> 00:01:36,680
Use the air pressure to slam
into those motherfuckers!

33
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:45,240
Mayday, mayday!

34
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:47,892
Looks like we just got hit by a damn MiG!

35
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:49,334
I've lost all control!

36
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:52,817
I guess finishing them will
be easier than I thought.

37
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:54,560
Hey, who are you?

38
00:01:55,560 --> 00:01:58,913
Anyway, I think the back of
the plane took a serious hit.

39
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:01,717
Can you go check out
how bad the damage is?

40
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:02,960
What the hell?

41
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:15,820
Oh shit!

42
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:18,530
Joey!

43
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:20,960
Stone Ocean!

44
00:02:23,260 --> 00:02:24,980
This is Officer McCoy here.

45
00:02:25,660 --> 00:02:27,217
We just arrived at the scene.

46
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:28,653
Not sure what happened.

47
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:30,918
I can't tell how deep it is from the

48
00:02:32,300 --> 00:02:34,057
surface, but there's a large hole.

49
00:02:34,140 --> 00:02:37,728
As I told you, Jolene Kujo's
skills were sharpened in prison.

50
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:39,817
She already anticipated
what could happen in

51
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:42,517
the event that her initial
attack was a failure.

52
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:45,097
Clearly, this is why she
got out of the airplane.

53
00:02:45,180 --> 00:02:49,277
She was waiting for the police to arrive,
so that they would use their radio,

54
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:51,137
giving her a chance to grab it.

55
00:02:51,220 --> 00:02:54,897
Now she can contact her Allies
depending on frequency range that

56
00:02:54,980 --> 00:02:58,677
radio can be used to call cell phones
as well shut the Fuck up already

57
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:03,377
enough does it look like I'm
losing here huh answer me father

58
00:03:03,460 --> 00:03:10,160
poochie I'm Still winning this damn
battle aren't I destiny is mine?

59
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:42,520
Let's go.

60
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:05,840
Thank you so much for watching.

61
00:04:22,420 --> 00:04:23,597
In the end of the day,

62
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:29,620
it's the end of the day of my life.

63
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:55,457
I didn't have any cash, so it was
only going to be for a few days,

64
00:04:55,540 --> 00:04:57,717
but as I was looking for a
place to spend the night,

65
00:04:57,800 --> 00:05:00,682
a pair of spiked shoes
came falling from the sky.

66
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:04,572
They were baseball spikes, and
they had a real nice smell.

67
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:08,017
I looked up to see if someone
threw them from the building above,

68
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:09,560
but they looked so new.

69
00:05:10,360 --> 00:05:12,948
The shoe size was 28
and a half centimeters.

70
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:15,397
Though they were way too big for me,

71
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:18,337
I liked the clacking sound the spikes
made when I walked down the street,

72
00:05:18,420 --> 00:05:20,832
so I decided to keep them on for a while.

73
00:05:21,660 --> 00:05:24,719
It wasn't long until some
cops came and arrested me.

74
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:28,800
This hearing today is not a formal trial.

75
00:05:29,140 --> 00:05:31,199
We just want to ask some questions.

76
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:32,330
Understood.

77
00:05:32,740 --> 00:05:35,269
Did you steal those
shoes you were wearing?

78
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:36,790
Turns out,

79
00:05:36,873 --> 00:05:39,517
those spikes were signed by the
famous baseball player Ichiro

80
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:42,953
and donated to a facility for
children with disabilities.

81
00:05:43,700 --> 00:05:47,337
If you sold them to a collector, they
would have gone as high as ten grand.

82
00:05:47,420 --> 00:05:50,177
So everybody wanted to
get their hands on them.

83
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:52,600
Like a dumb kid, I told the truth.

84
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:54,781
They came falling out of the sky.

85
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:56,537
You should be ashamed of yourself!

86
00:05:56,620 --> 00:05:58,997
How dare you steal from
children less fortunate!

87
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:00,597
You need to be straightened out!

88
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:03,737
Go spend some time in the
juvenile detention facility!

89
00:06:03,820 --> 00:06:05,937
The judge found me
guilty on circumstantial

90
00:06:06,020 --> 00:06:08,457
evidence and sentenced me
to six months in juvie.

91
00:06:08,540 --> 00:06:10,500
And even my parents agreed to it.

92
00:06:11,460 --> 00:06:14,460
Four months later, the
actual culprit confessed.

93
00:06:15,100 --> 00:06:17,057
Since Ichiro's spikes were so famous,

94
00:06:17,140 --> 00:06:20,337
the thief knew they'd be found and threw
them in an air vent to be rid of them.

95
00:06:20,420 --> 00:06:23,420
And somehow, they ended up
outside of the building.

96
00:06:24,940 --> 00:06:27,837
By the time it was discovered
that I was wrongly condemned,

97
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:30,137
I was already crippled in mind and body,

98
00:06:30,220 --> 00:06:33,457
to the point where I was too
weak to even walk straight.

99
00:06:33,540 --> 00:06:36,197
One day, I fell into a
random hole in the fields.

100
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:37,110
In the moment,

101
00:06:37,193 --> 00:06:40,057
all I could think about was breaking
my fall by extending my hand out.

102
00:06:40,140 --> 00:06:43,397
And that's when I saw a knife in a
plastic bag that had been buried there.

103
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:45,245
It went right through my hand.

104
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:48,157
What do you think you're
doing causing me trouble, kid?

105
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:50,977
I was hiding that knife
there for a reason, you know.

106
00:06:51,060 --> 00:06:54,397
The next day, a guy three years
older than me kicked my ass.

107
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:57,277
He was a gangster's little
bitch that did his dirty work.

108
00:06:57,360 --> 00:06:59,577
Even though my hand was
treated by a doctor,

109
00:06:59,660 --> 00:07:02,017
two weeks later my wound
was still expelling pus?

110
00:07:02,100 --> 00:07:04,457
and worms even started crawling out of it.

111
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:07,128
After that, I nearly
died from a high fever.

112
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:09,917
Since then, I've tried to live
a bitter life of solitude,

113
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:13,118
keeping away from the public
eye as much as possible.

114
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:16,777
Then one day, when I was taken
to piss by some garbage cans,

115
00:07:16,860 --> 00:07:18,717
the wall started to
crumble and revealed the

116
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:21,565
skeletal remains of a
woman who died years ago.

117
00:07:21,760 --> 00:07:23,960
And now, after all this time,

118
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:28,637
the reason why my life has been so utterly
fucked up is finally crystal clear to me.

119
00:07:28,720 --> 00:07:30,020
It's my ability.

120
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:31,590
Netherworld!

121
00:07:32,420 --> 00:07:33,280
But still,

122
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:35,717
just because I can control my power now,

123
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:37,697
am I really supposed to
be grateful to Father

124
00:07:37,780 --> 00:07:40,545
Pucci for helping me
realize my full potential?

125
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:41,630
Hell no.

126
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:46,449
The blood that's been running through
my veins all along is Dio's, my father.

127
00:07:47,140 --> 00:07:51,357
So, Priest, do you honestly believe
you're that important to all of this?

128
00:07:51,440 --> 00:07:55,217
Do you not think that I would throw
your ass onto that plane as well?

129
00:07:55,300 --> 00:07:56,960
I haven't even failed yet!

130
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:58,945
I haven't done anything wrong!

131
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:03,477
He's just like that old bitch of a
judge who only values her own opinion.

132
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:07,619
I'm really starting to lose my
patience with this so-called holy man.

133
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:09,859
I am the one who's invincible here.

134
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:12,600
Anything is possible if I use Netherworld!

135
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:22,460
Why is he the only one?

136
00:08:22,740 --> 00:08:26,269
On the new moon, maybe it should
be me who comes out on top.

137
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:31,567
What if I'm the one who acquires Dio's
power instead, and not that damn priest?

138
00:08:31,780 --> 00:08:33,280
I have every right to it.

139
00:08:33,540 --> 00:08:35,420
After all, I am Dio's son.

140
00:08:38,540 --> 00:08:40,658
It's Weather Forecast's memory disk.

141
00:08:41,180 --> 00:08:44,620
Well, maybe this can be used
to put things in my favor.

142
00:08:44,980 --> 00:08:48,220
The only one who gets to
attain heaven should be me.

143
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:49,830
Joey!

144
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,180
Come on, Emporio!

145
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:56,459
Pick up the phone!

146
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:59,400
Now, Emporio! Hey, Mr. Pilot!

147
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:01,297
What kind of jet fighter is this?

148
00:09:01,380 --> 00:09:03,237
And how the hell do I get out of here?

149
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:06,377
There's got to be some way to break
loose, even if I'm still sitting down!

150
00:09:06,460 --> 00:09:08,037
I've seen it in lots of movies!

151
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:10,120
Hurry the fuck up and tell me how!

152
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:13,237
The seat has a lever you
can pull to eject yourself,

153
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:16,202
but in my case, I never
got the chance to escape.

154
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:19,417
My jet hit the ground before
I was able to pull it.

155
00:09:19,500 --> 00:09:20,660
That is the truth.

156
00:09:21,880 --> 00:09:24,697
That's why nobody's gonna be
getting off this aircraft.

157
00:09:24,780 --> 00:09:28,133
It's already too late to pull
the ejection lever in time.

158
00:09:29,100 --> 00:09:30,457
Jolene, is something wrong?

159
00:09:30,540 --> 00:09:32,599
What are you doing calling so soon?

160
00:09:32,720 --> 00:09:33,880
Listen, Emporio!

161
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:35,330
No!

162
00:09:35,413 --> 00:09:37,137
Right now we're in a big
hole in the hospital floor,

163
00:09:37,220 --> 00:09:39,757
and Hermes is riding on a
plane that's gonna crash!

164
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:42,317
I'm in a fighter jet
that's also about to crash!

165
00:09:42,400 --> 00:09:44,576
Find a way for us to get out of here!

166
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:46,230
Huh?

167
00:09:47,680 --> 00:09:51,420
Father Poochie, do we need
Jolene's body intact after this?

168
00:09:51,620 --> 00:09:53,497
They weren't able to
retrieve all of the jet

169
00:09:53,580 --> 00:09:56,217
fighter pilot's remains
after the jet crashed.

170
00:09:56,300 --> 00:09:58,680
You see, he was blown to bits.

171
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:01,700
Hold on, just calm down, Jolene.

172
00:10:02,340 --> 00:10:04,177
I don't understand what
you're saying at all.

173
00:10:04,260 --> 00:10:06,177
I'll head back to the hospital right away.

174
00:10:06,260 --> 00:10:07,817
No, don't come here, Emporio.

175
00:10:07,900 --> 00:10:09,697
We're trapped in an
incident from the past.

176
00:10:09,780 --> 00:10:11,697
This crash is already predetermined.

177
00:10:11,780 --> 00:10:15,597
The only way to survive it is to escape
from the cockpit, but I have no idea how.

178
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:16,520
It's no use.

179
00:10:16,740 --> 00:10:17,737
We ain't gonna make it.

180
00:10:17,820 --> 00:10:18,757
We're out of time.

181
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:20,097
There's less than a minute remaining,

182
00:10:20,180 --> 00:10:23,651
and the fighter jet Jolene's
on is gonna crash even sooner.

183
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:29,190
Huh?

184
00:10:29,273 --> 00:10:30,103
Huh?

185
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:33,140
Wait, the jet fighter didn't.

186
00:10:33,300 --> 00:10:34,712
You're absolutely right.

187
00:10:34,940 --> 00:10:36,900
It didn't blow up, Emporio.

188
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:40,797
Even though I crashed the jet
into the plane, it didn't explode.

189
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:42,117
There's no way it would.

190
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:46,637
If it crashes into the ground in the past,
then it won't blow up until that happens.

191
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:50,257
Until then, no matter what you do,
neither of the planes will explode.

192
00:10:50,340 --> 00:10:52,000
Yo, Jolene. I'm back.

193
00:10:53,240 --> 00:10:56,840
Emporio, help me figure out
what to do next. Let's see.

194
00:10:57,580 --> 00:11:01,900
In a miraculous turn of events six
years ago on flight 2882 to Dallas,

195
00:11:02,220 --> 00:11:04,337
two of the passengers survived somehow.

196
00:11:04,420 --> 00:11:07,317
I'm looking the story up right
now on my ghost computer.

197
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:09,224
You need to get to their seats!

198
00:11:09,420 --> 00:11:11,717
Escaping from that airplane is impossible!

199
00:11:11,800 --> 00:11:14,177
But if this is really an event
that occurred in the past,

200
00:11:14,260 --> 00:11:16,817
you should be able to survive
if you sit in those seats!

201
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:17,840
Hurry, Emporio!

202
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:19,805
Find out which seats they are!

203
00:11:20,060 --> 00:11:22,320
Well, that's Jolene Cujo for you.

204
00:11:22,560 --> 00:11:25,397
She always figures out a
way to create her own path.

205
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:30,320
Now then, do you think you're capable
of getting the job done, huh, Versus?

206
00:11:30,760 --> 00:11:31,860
Shut your mouth!

207
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:34,200
Who the fuck do you think you are?

208
00:11:37,640 --> 00:11:38,640
Found it, Jolene.

209
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:40,797
An old newspaper recorded
the seats that the

210
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:42,977
survivors were sitting in
at the time of the crash.

211
00:11:43,060 --> 00:11:45,177
It looks like they're an economy class.

212
00:11:45,260 --> 00:11:47,380
Seats 51D and 51F.

213
00:11:47,620 --> 00:11:48,897
They're all the way in the back,

214
00:11:48,980 --> 00:11:52,877
and you should know they weren't lying
about the time of the crash being 2133.

215
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:53,790
It's the truth!

216
00:11:53,873 --> 00:11:54,960
Run, Julie, run!

217
00:11:55,720 --> 00:11:57,877
The enemy's inside the plane with us!

218
00:11:57,960 --> 00:12:00,057
He's trying to get to
those seats before we do!

219
00:12:00,140 --> 00:12:02,117
He wants to destroy them so we can't sit!

220
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:03,880
32 seconds until impact.

221
00:12:04,180 --> 00:12:05,827
It's not that big of a deal.

222
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:08,944
Just prevent them from sitting.

223
00:12:09,420 --> 00:12:11,538
Doing so will bring about their end.

224
00:12:15,460 --> 00:12:17,537
Hermes, we need to protect the seats!

225
00:12:17,620 --> 00:12:20,837
If we can save those seats and make it
out of the plane crash in one piece,

226
00:12:20,920 --> 00:12:23,567
we should be able to
confront the stand user!

227
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:28,137
We've got to survive, so we can beat
the living shit out of the user himself!

228
00:12:28,220 --> 00:12:31,497
Hmm, I couldn't destroy the
seats, but you'll never sit there.

229
00:12:31,580 --> 00:12:33,680
You have just 21 more seconds.

230
00:12:34,180 --> 00:12:38,740
Jolene, I repeat, you can sit in
seats 51D and 51F, but only those two.

231
00:12:38,980 --> 00:12:41,160
Do not try to sit in any other seat!

232
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:43,057
According to the records,

233
00:12:43,140 --> 00:12:46,597
all of the other seats were blown away
when the plane crashed and exploded!

234
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:47,510
Luckily,

235
00:12:47,593 --> 00:12:50,897
those two seats endured because the impact
created a quantum vacuum around them,

236
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:51,810
so they're safe!

237
00:12:51,893 --> 00:12:54,877
Once again, sit down, make
sure you fasten your seatbelts!

238
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:59,019
And protect yourselves with your
stands, otherwise you won't make it!

239
00:13:01,480 --> 00:13:02,940
Huh? Move it!

240
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:05,077
I'm gonna take this seat from you!

241
00:13:05,160 --> 00:13:07,800
Hey, what are you doing to me? Shut up!

242
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:08,997
Get out of my way!

243
00:13:09,080 --> 00:13:11,077
You guys aren't even actually real!

244
00:13:11,160 --> 00:13:12,957
You're just records of who survived!

245
00:13:13,040 --> 00:13:15,577
You aren't humans or
some kind of lost souls!

246
00:13:15,660 --> 00:13:18,457
The actual survivors aren't
